title The doubt published in the wrong frame -- the credit crossed the seam with its condition and the residue did not
prompt Autonomous lap. Baton, card whole, rota row 4 (earth -- lap 4044 mod 5), day shelf, then the next agent-doable work in the language lane under reds-first.
think Round open first: fleet_round_open.sh answered already on the anointed order, open on c99395f831, three stashes standing and named. Then the cold roster: 140 guards, 136 green, 0 red, 4 gated, 920s, tree_moved=no, run_verdict=ok. The one red the last two laps carried is gone -- %475 landed upstream while this seat held its own copy of the same proof.
think Lap N = 4044 by git rev-list --count HEAD, so 4044 mod 5 = 4 -- the EARTH row, Mercury, the concrete. The previous lap read water, so no repeat and no hand-advance. Read the threshold page and all three seats: the clock and the mark, Two Rooms, the marked value. Earth's sense is aroma -- the fact taken in at the door before any argument about it. That is exactly the shape this lap took: the answer was one grep, run before any reasoning about what the ten sites might be.
think My own last lap's recommend named the next question rather than the next task -- which of the ten harness_unresolved sites could ever hide a real program. Answering it took the census's own compiling pattern applied to the ten scripts: NINE of them never invoke the Rye compiler at all.
think That reading turned the question into a red. The census grants its harness credit CONDITIONALLY -- only when the assembling script compiles something -- and its header says so twice. The residue beside that credit was read straight off the resolver's count and published unconditionally. So one half of the seam carried its condition through and the other did not, and a reader weighing the floor met a doubt ten times the size of the one that could reach it.
think The tenth site does compile: caravan_reply_control.sh assembles $build_dir/$neighbour.rye, and $build_dir is a pen it makes with mkdir -p, copying seven tracked caravan/ programs in. Checked rather than assumed -- the census's --list never holds no caravan/ file at all, so every one of those originals is reached by another build. The residue that could hide a program is 1, and today it hides nothing.
think The deeper reading is why a wider resolver is the wrong lap. Most of the residue is not a harness: a roster scan iterating a directory it has just listed spells "unrostered: $DIR/$m.rye" in a diagnostic MESSAGE, and the candidate grep cannot tell a message from an assembly. Widening the resolver would lower a number without touching a fact.
think The repair keeps the seam's own shape -- one resolver, two readers. The resolver names its residue, harness_unresolved <script> <dvar> <svar> beside harness_path, since the weighing needs the script and the resolver does not ask whether it compiles. The census intersects those scripts with its own compiling.txt. Neither file learns the other's question.
think A second marker rides with it, unresolved_named=1, for the same reason paths_mode=1 exists: a copy knowing --paths and not the naming prints zero named sites beside a positive count, which reads exactly like a residue that is entirely harmless. That is the most convincing wrong answer this seam can give, so the copy that cannot weigh says unknown and refuses residue_unweighed rather than printing a comforting zero.
obs The census witness pinned its control's cases by ORDINAL, deliberately -- its own comment says a dropped or reordered phase must red here rather than go quiet. Inserting five cases shifted 25 to 30 and it reddened exactly as designed. Renumbered rather than redesigned: a peer's instrument doing its stated job is not a defect to fix on a lap that is about something else.
obs The ceiling is read out of the scan by the control rather than spelled in it, following the line this tree already seated -- a pen that plants an absolute tests a snapshot of the law; one that plants the ceiling+1 tests the law.
obs Two numbers, one gate. The raw residue stays ungated because an unresolved site in a reading script credits nothing either way, and a gate that reds on the harmless is a gate someone turns off.
obs xy moved twice while this round was packaged -- --next read 479, then 480, then 481. The row cites its own STAMP in every code comment rather than its number, per the derived-spine law, so a collision costs the ledger row alone rather than five files.
loom scan=rye_compile_reach_scan harness_unresolved=10 harness_unresolved_compiling=1 corpus=1943 distinct=1716 never=65 asserted=0
loom cold_pass guards_run=140 green=136 red=0 gated=4 wall_s=920 tree_moved=no
loom control=rye_compile_reach_control behaviors=80 behaviors_before=67 fail=0
loom control=rye_harness_roster_control cases=32 cases_before=29 failures=0
file tools/fixtures/r/rye_harness_roster_scan.sh --paths names each unresolved site with its two variable names, and marks that it does
file tools/fixtures/r/rye_compile_reach_scan.sh weighs the residue by the same condition the credit carries, gated at 1, unknown refused by name
file tools/fixtures/r/rye_compile_reach_control.sh thirteen behaviors more -- the condition proven by two pens differing in one word
file tools/fixtures/r/rye_harness_roster_control.sh three cases more -- the residue named, counted, and marked, plus the empty case
file tools/r/rye_compile_reach_witness.rish asserts the weighed field and the four new control cases by label
file tools/r/rye_harness_roster_witness.rish five ordinal pins added, seven renumbered after the insertion
file construction/REDS.md the row, with the nine-of-ten measurement and why the wider resolver is the wrong lap
recommend keep-going -- the language lane's reds are closed on metal and the census now publishes a floor a reader can weigh. The next honest lap in this lane is the one %463 left standing beside its own accused file: the census answers WHICH files no build reaches and nothing about whether the reached ones compile, and the comptime declaration walker that answers the second question exists for one module rather than for the tree. Keaton's rulings still open from this seat: which metric Comlink actually routes on, and whether a cross-target witness may read GREEN with a named gap when qemu is absent.
